From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:26:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: use a 64-bit DMA mask

brcmfmac never sets a DMA mask, so the PCI default of 32 bits applies,
although every ring and buffer descriptor it hands the dongle carries a
64-bit host address (msgbuf_buf_addr high_addr/low_addr). Google's
driver for the same chips sets a 64-bit mask (bcmdhd dhd_pcie_linux.c
dhdpcie_pci_probe(), DMA_BIT_MASK(64)).

With a restricted DMA pool (reserved-memory "restricted-dma-pool") every
coherent allocation is carved from the pool, and dma-direct rejects the
pool if it is not reachable under the coherent mask. On the Pixel 7 Pro
the 16 MiB pool is placed at 0xaff000000, so all allocations failed:
the DMA index buffer silently ("Using TCM indices"), then the first
common ring:

  brcmf_pcie_init_ringbuffers: Allocating ring buffers failed

Ask for 64 bits and fall back to 32. Hosts that cannot address all of
it describe that with dma-ranges on the bridge, which the DMA core
applies on top of the mask.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c   | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index 1c5961036..c9431c81e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/bcma/bcma.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
@@ -2017,6 +2018,20 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_get_resource(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo)
 
 	pci_set_master(pdev);
 
+	/* The dongle takes 64-bit host addresses in every ring and buffer
+	 * descriptor. Without this the PCI default 32-bit mask applies, and
+	 * every allocation from a restricted DMA pool placed above 4 GiB
+	 * fails.
+	 */
+	err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	if (err) {
+		err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+		if (err) {
+			brcmf_err(bus, "no usable DMA mask: %d\n", err);
+			return err;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* Bar-0 mapped address */
 	bar0_addr = pci_resource_start(pdev, 0);
 	/* Bar-1 mapped address */
